<title>USA: Exxon full year EPS raised.</title>
<headline>Exxon full year EPS raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Morgan Grenfell analyst Michael Young as raised his 1997 full year earnings per share forecast for Exxon Corp by 10 cents to $3.15 and 1998 by 10 cents to $3.15 after the company reported second quarter earnings ahead of forecasts.</p>
<p>Exxon reported EPS of $0.79 compared with $0.63 a year ago and the stock was up 14/16 at 61-5/16 in volume of 1,788,600 shares. ((-- David Chance New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
</text>
